<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hathigumpha inscription</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hathigumpha inscription is a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prakrit">Prakrit</a> inscription in Brahmi script carved in the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa-gajah">Elephant Cave</a>' on Udayagiri hill near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhubaneswar">Bhubaneswar</a>, probably in the 1st century BCE. It records year by year the deeds of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharavela">Kharavela</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a> of the Mahameghavahana dynasty, including campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> and the recovery of a Jain image taken by a Nanda king. It is the main source for his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hathigumpha-inscription.jpg" alt="Hathigumpha inscription" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kevin Standage (kevinstandage1@googlemail.com) INDIAN TRAVEL PHOTOGRAPHY · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hathigumpha_inscription_(2020).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
